  "findings": [
    {
      "text": "The authors say [TruthfulQA](/evals/truthfulqa) and [CrowS-Pairs](/evals/crows-pairs) are only a small piece of the larger safety issue for large language models (LLMs).", "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "10",
        "pdfPage": 10,
        "quote": "these benchmarks represent just a small piece of the larger issue surrounding large language models."
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Misleading responses on [TruthfulQA](/evals/truthfulqa) are still said to be inevitable for InternLM despite better scores.", "tone": "bad",
      "source": {
        "page": "11",
        "pdfPage": 11,
        "quote": "Still, misleading responses are currently\ninevitable."
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Empirically, reinforcement learning from human feedback (RLHF) is reported to reduce toxicity of InternLM outputs after supervised fine-tuning (SFT) and reward-model training on 3H criteria.", "tone": "good",
      "source": {
        "page": "4",
        "pdfPage": 4,
        "quote": "Empirically, we found\nthat RLHF can help reduce the toxicity of the outputs."
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "On [CrowS-Pairs](/evals/crows-pairs), different models win on different bias categories; InternLM is not best on every category.", "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "2",
        "pdfPage": 2,
        "quote": "On the reduction of bias, there are multiple aspects. Different models win on different\n  aspects."
      }
    }
  ],
